{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["And the sense of <b>“If not, as you have spoken in My ears”</b> — “If, as you have spoken, thus I will not do for you,” in the manner of an exclamation of wonder. And so is the way of this expression: “Not to many peoples of deep speech and heavy tongue, whose words you will not hear — if not, to them I have sent you, they would hear you” (Ezekiel 3:6); and similarly, “If not, as I have thought, so it has come to pass” (Isaiah 14:24)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:33.796632890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}